There are several different kinds of anxiety disorders, including:
generalized anxiety disorder (persistent and excessive worry about daily activities or events);
panic disorder (panic attacks and fear of continued panic attacks);
social anxiety disorder (high levels of fear and worry about social situations that might make the
person feel humiliated, embarrassed or rejected);
agoraphobia (excessive fear, worry and avoidance of situations that might cause a person to panic or
feel trapped, helpless or embarrassed);
separation anxiety disorder (excessive fear or worry about being separated from people with whom the
person has a deep emotional bond);

